 SA News Editor Apple (NASDAQ: AAPL ) is investing $1B in a new campus in Austin, Texas, that will have capacity for 15K employees and make it the largest private employer in the city. The company also announced plans to establish new sites in Seattle, San Diego and Culver City and expand in Pittsburgh, New York and Boulder, Colorado. Apple added 6K jobs to its American workforce in 2018 and now employs 90K people in all 50 states. It intends to create 20K U.S. jobs by 2023.", "external_links": ["https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2018/12/apple-to-build-new-campus-in-austin-and-add-jobs-across-the-us/"], "published": "2018-12-13T10:33:00.000+02:00", "crawled": "2018-12-13T11:24:28.015+02:00", "highlightTitle": ""}